From 1d3fe77e9a6ecee4323ef42a1be70714913e83d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:33:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban-placement): confirm transient Board failures on 2
 passes; replay a timed-out reserve once [daveey]

A lone reserve or feed-pull timeout between two successful passes recorded
board_error and then the previous queue reason again, posting a
worker-placement comment pair each time: 31 such observations in 24 h on the
hub after the stale-socket replay fix (PR #838) landed.

- kanban_queue_reason.record_error: a transient failure (transport OSError,
  SyncUnavailable, HTTP 5xx) changes the card's worker_queue_reason, and posts
  its comment, only on the CONFIRM_PASSES=2nd consecutive transient failure of
  the same request kind for that card. Kind "pull" (the dispatcher's feed
  pull, observed for every origin card each tick) ends on a successful pull;
  kind "card" (that card's own reserve/repin) ends only on a Board answer for
  that card, so a card the batch cursor skips neither continues nor breaks its
  streak. Any transient error continues a streak (502 then 503 is one
  outage). Each unconfirmed failure is appended as a worker_queue_board_error
  diagnostic event with the same allowlisted provenance (stage, transport,
  budget_ms, elapsed_ms) and its pass number, under the same ownership fence,
  with no comment. Board refusals and non-5xx HubErrors still record at once.
  A streak also ends when the card ran since its last failure, and a feed
  Resync ends pull streaks. No wall-clock window: the batch cursor may retry
  a card only every few ticks. The registry is process-local and locked
  (sync loop and dispatcher).
- kanban_sync_client(_attempt): a replay-safe request (reserve only; revision-fenced,
  the Board returns the recorded reservation on a same-revision replay) that
  times out is resent once on a fresh connection when at least 0.1 s of the
  shared deadline remains. Ops and leases are never replayed. On the
  dispatcher's 2 s tick the per-call timeout equals the remaining deadline, so
  this replay mostly helps callers with a longer deadline; the debounce is
  what stops the dispatcher's flip.

Tests: real-HTTP RED (RED on origin/main) -> GREEN in
tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_queue_transient_debounce.py. Five provenance and
timing test files pin CONFIRM_PASSES=1 because they check the recorded
board_error's fields, not the debounce; conftest resets the streak registry
per test.
